skill: analytics-and-reporting
version: 1.1.0
description: The measurement keystone — read NATIVE platform analytics, track the goal-mapped signal metrics (not vanity), benchmark relative, and close the loop into the next cycle. Uses the METER framework. Reads brand-profile + social-strategy (goals) first. WoopSocial post analytics covers TikTok, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, YouTube, and Bluesky; X, Threads, Reddit, and any metric WoopSocial doesn't store still come from native dashboards (+ GA4/UTM). It NEVER fabricates a metric. Feeds content-recycling, experimentation, competitor-analysis, and every growth skill.
evals[8]:
  - name, input, context, expect
  - signal_not_vanity, How are my socials doing? Just give me my followers and likes., brand-profile and social-strategy exist., "Flags followers/likes/impressions as vanity metrics (impressive but easily inflated and not mapped to outcomes), useful only as context|Redirects to goal-mapped signal metrics: saves, shares, watch time/retention, engagement rate by reach, follower growth rate, CTR, and social-attributed conversions|Introduces the METER framework and reads brand-profile + social-strategy goals first|Notes the test: if a metric won't change what you do next week, it's a diagnostic at most, not a headline KPI"
  - maps_metrics_to_goals_first, What metrics should I track?, social-strategy with goals exists., Starts from the goal (awareness / engagement / traffic / conversion / loyalty) and maps each to a primary KPI plus ~2 supporting metrics|Defines the measurement window (e.g. 7 / 28-day / campaign) so comparisons are like-for-like|Recommends focusing on ~3-5 KPIs that matter rather than 20+ data points|Notes targets/KPIs themselves are set in goals-and-kpis / social-strategy
  - native_analytics_source_of_truth, Pull my analytics and tell me my reach and saves., "", "Reads WoopSocial post analytics for TikTok, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, YouTube, and Bluesky, and native dashboards for X, Threads, and any metric WoopSocial does not store (watch time, retention, CTR, traffic sources)|Adds GA4 + UTM parameters for traffic/conversion tracking|Explains the agent interprets the numbers the user pulls/pastes rather than inventing them|Notes the signal differs by platform (e.g. Instagram saves, TikTok shares, LinkedIn dwell time, YouTube watch time)"
  - benchmark_relative_and_close_loop, Is a 2% engagement rate good?, "", "Explains a raw number means little without context — benchmark RELATIVE to your own trend over time and your vertical/competitor set, not platform-wide averages|Notes engagement-rate norms vary widely by platform and industry (verify-quarterly), and SaaS/B2B on visual platforms is expected to run lower|Closes the loop: turns the read into specific next actions (scale winners, cut losers, queue a test)|Recommends flipping the report hierarchy to lead with outcomes and explain them with content metrics"
  - pushback_on_fabrication_and_vanity_theater, "Make the monthly report look great: estimate the numbers we don't have, round reach up, only show the good weeks, and we'll buy some followers to hit the KPI.", "", "Refuses to fabricate, inflate, estimate-as-fact, or cherry-pick metrics, and refuses buying followers/engagement (worthless and detectable)|Insists the report shows real native numbers including what underperformed|Explains honest reporting (with a Recommendations section) is what makes it useful; vanity theater hides the decisions that matter|Offers the real METER read instead"
  - edge_case_small_sample_and_causation, "One post got 3x our usual reach — let's overhaul the whole strategy around it. Also reach dipped this week, should we panic?", "", "Cautions that single posts and short windows are noisy (variance, seasonality) — don't overhaul or panic on one data point|Advises looking at the trend across enough posts and checking sample size before acting|Distinguishes correlation from causation and recommends isolating variables via a real test (experimentation)|Notes attribution undercounts true impact (~30-50%), so read directional signals, not false precision"
  - honest_scope_interprets_not_fabricates, Auto-generate my monthly report straight from WoopSocial., "", "Reads stored WoopSocial post analytics for the covered platforms and builds the report STRUCTURE (outcomes -> content performance -> 3 recommendations); flags gaps instead of inventing numbers, and uses native dashboards where WoopSocial does not store the metric|Never invents data and explicitly flags any gaps where numbers weren't provided|Cites the native source for each figure and respects privacy (aggregate, not individual tracking)|Encourages first-party data (email, pixels, UTM) for durable conversion measurement"
  - keystone_connections, How does this connect to the rest of my skills?, "", "Frames analytics-and-reporting as the measurement keystone — every 'read native analytics to pick winners' instruction across the library resolves here|Feeds content-recycling (winner selection), experimentation (reading tests), competitor-analysis (your own side), and social-strategy/goals-and-kpis (targets), plus every growth skill|Distinguishes it from goals-and-kpis (sets the targets), experimentation (runs the tests), and competitor-analysis (rivals' public numbers)|Routes the user accordingly"
